<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Six Articles (1832)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1832</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Six Articles were repressive measures adopted by the Federal Assembly of the German Confederation on 28 June 1832, after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hambach-festival">Hambach Festival</a>. Promoted by Metternich, they restricted the rights of state parliaments to refuse taxes or legislate against federal law and set up a commission to watch over them. Further decrees banned political associations and public meetings.</p></div>
